  "howTo": [
    "Writes right to left, and the keys follow the Israeli PC layout: A is ש, E is ק. Q types ת, and W types ', for words like צ'יפס. Hold P for ף, M for ץ, and Q for /. Hebrew has no capitals, so Shift types the same letter. The bar reads right to left too: the best word stays in the middle, the next one on the right."
  ],
